WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.002
Joining us now, the Republican governor

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.636
of New Hampshire, Chris Sununu,

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.006
a vocal Trump critic who has endorsed

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.340
Nikki Haley for president.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.075
Governor, thanks so much for joining us,

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:09.709
first of all.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.578
Do you condemn what we just heard

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.013
from Trump in your own state

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.447
that immigrants are, quote,

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.449
poisoning the blood of our country,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.650
seemingly echoing

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.920
Adolf Hitler and white supremacists?

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.588
It's awful.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.789
It's absolutely awful.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.224
But unfortunately, with Donald Trump,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.392
it shouldn't be surprising.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.259
And there's a couple of reason

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.394
he's doing it. He's doing it.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.362
He knows that Nikki is gaining on him,

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.730
especially here in New Hampshire.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.232
He wants to spur up that that

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.533
negative evil rhetoric

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.602
to kind of get his extremists of his base

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.970
to make sure that they're not leaving him

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.405
because a lot of his other voters

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:39.606
are likely to move from him

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:40.640
in the next couple of weeks.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.474
But most importantly,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.210
what he's doing is he wants he wants to

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.478
hopefully not let folks

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.579
ask him the question of,

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.048
hey, why don't you secure the border

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.282
like you promised you do?

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.083
He's almost acting

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.117
like he wasn't president.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:51.351
Right.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:51.584
Remember,

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.119
he said he was going to build the wall

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.287
and make Mexico pay for it

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.622
and secure the border and all that.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.623
He didn't do any of it.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:57.557
And now we have this

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.825
crisis coming in to our country,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.026
which most Republicans

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.261
and most folks across the country

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.595
want that border secure.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.164
So he's going to spur up the rhetoric

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.498
because he's not taking questions,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.900
not answering anything,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.401
not getting on the debate stage.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.202
And he wants to make sure

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.770
that that base is with him.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.572
It's an awful way to do it.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.640
It speaks more to

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.574
him and his character

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.842
and the problems you're going to have

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.177
if he were elected again

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.445
and which is why, Nikki,

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.679
that type of stuff is why

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.014
Nikki Haley is surging here

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.514
in New Hampshire.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.083
I think she's going to be surging

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.950
in Iowa.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.251
It's not a 40 point race.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.553
It's a 15 point race.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.754
And I think pretty soon

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.121
you're going to see

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.422
it's about a two point race

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.223
and a real tossup

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.891
between Haley and Trump going forward.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:32.759
We shall see.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.095
You've endorsed Nikki Haley,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.729
who so far, governor, as

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:36.996
you know,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.665
has not denounced Trump's

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.601
authoritarian and very hateful rhetoric.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.136
This should be simple to condemn.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.939
So why hasn't she?

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:46.773
Well, look, I mean, I'm

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:47.607
not going to speak for Nikki

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.842
other than to say when she's out there.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.477
She talks about the former president.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.077
She talks that

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.345
this is the time to move on.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.013
There's no there's no place for that.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.215
But I think she does a good job

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.150
of making sure that she's not just saying

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.118
elect me for president

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.252
because we don't like that guy.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.987
Elect me because of that rhetoric.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.856
She's putting her resume, her

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.257
her background, her experience,

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.225
and most importantly,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.593
what she's going to bring.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.027
She she's a former governor.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.829
So it's not just about political points

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:10.663
and policy.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.098
It's about actually achieving

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.399
something, accountability,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.701
how you manage the government,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.835
how you manage getting things

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.337
done, how you work with Congress.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:17.904
And again,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.972
that type of message

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.607
is really resonating with folks.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.841
They don't want to live in the past

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.408
here in New Hampshire.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:22.809
New Hampshire's

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.310
always a forward looking state,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.745
which is why she's doing so well.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.813
But don't you think she should

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:31.518
denounce Trump's hateful rhetoric?

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.652
Well, look, I think I think

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.753
she's been pretty hard on him.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.320
I do.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:34.921
I again,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:35.722
I think everybody's

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.090
waiting for every candidate

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.891
to go nuclear,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.992
kind of like Chris Christie does.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.760
And Chris has done a great job of that.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.895
I think I'm out there doing it.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:42.896
But, you know,

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:43.563
not everyone's

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.765
going to have the exact same style.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.067
Their folks say, well, you're too

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.536
too much pro-Trump and, you know,

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.670
go hard on him enough.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.471
Other folks say,

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.639
oh, you're too anti-Trump

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.973
and why can't you like him more?

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.807
So she's right

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.176
where she needs to be as a candidate,

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.477
which is talking about the future.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.211
So, no, I

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.213
if I thought she was doing it wrong,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:00.947
if I thought it wasn't

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:01.781
resonating with folks,

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.916
I'd be the first to say it.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.185
But her style, her approach,

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.452
her background and likability

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.754
is what's really connecting with folks,

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.821
as you point out,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.690
Governor, in that CBS poll,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.092
Nikki Haley is surging to second place

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.561
in your state of New Hampshire.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.062
What do you think it would take

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:19.532
for her to close that gap?

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:20.366
Well, a couple of things.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.501
I think you're going to see a lot of

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.936
I mean, I think Chris Christie and Ron

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.404
DeSantis have run good races.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.538
They're great candidates.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.206
But you're going to see

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.040
a lot of those folks

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.608
start to start moving this way.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:29.776
New Hampshire wants to make sure

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:30.443
that we're the state

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.945
that doesn't live in the past.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.279
You're going to see a lot of those voters

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.347
come this way,

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.582
whether they get out of the race or not,

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.449
that's really up to them.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.051
But their voters are going to move

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.285
and even Trump voters,

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.620
the number one reason

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.621
why Trump voters say

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.823
they're going to vote for Trump is, well,

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.757
he's going to win anyway,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.292
so I guess we'll just vote for him.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.961
So you folks think it's inevitable?

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.796
So when we get out of kind of break

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.297
that mindset of it's inevitable

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.699
that there is somebody here

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.633
that's going to challenge him

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.235
that can hit the reset button

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.302
on the whole campaign

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.503
across the whole country,

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.871
that gets people excited.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.273
You have a lot of undeclared voters

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.741
coming out, a lot of the hardcore base

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.375
coming out

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.444
for a new version of the conservative

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.979
leadership, a new generation

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.213
that gets people excited.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.581
So it's just about working

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.349
the process

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.750
as folks are making up their minds.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.185
And that's what the next five weeks are.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.052
They're really starting

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.053
to make up their minds

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.088
whether it's over,

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.556
you know, the holidays with family

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.258
or interacting with coworkers,

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.592
or just coming out to see

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.193
Nikki Haley

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.694
one on one at one of our town halls.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:22.762
They've been tremendous.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.830
And it's making waves.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.498
This clearly is a critical moment

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.300
in this entire election cycle.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.301
Governor Chris Sununu,

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:31.070
thank you so much for joining us.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:31.838
You bet.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.071
All right.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.139
Let's get some more on all of this

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.207
with our political experts.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.808
And Gloria, let me start with you.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.676
What was your analysis

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.077
of what we just heard from governor?

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.045
Well, he's a cheerleader.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.113
He's a great cheerleader

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.681
for for Nikki Haley.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.448
And I think he made

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.783
some some good points,

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.985
which is about the inevitability

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.220
of Donald Trump.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.589
Lots of voters believe that, well,

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.623
maybe I'll vote for him

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.325
because he's going to win anyway.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.260
And I think he has the best chance

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.595
of beating Joe Biden.

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.063
And polls have shown

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.898
that may not be the case,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.500
that he's not inevitable,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.201
that Nikki Haley is moving up.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.469
And if they have a good reason

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.470
to leave Donald Trump,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.271
maybe they'll do it.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:07.106
Now, this is the rosy picture

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.308
that he paints.

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.409
But I think he also made

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.643
another interesting point,

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.279
which is about Donald Trump's behavior.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:13.680
Yes.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.380
As you point out,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.349
Nikki Haley is not attacking Donald Trump

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:18.451
the way, for example, he did.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.719
But the point that he made is

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.219
that Donald

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.354
Trump is acting

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:24.357
like he wasn't president before and that,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.191
you know, problems

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:25.825
at the border

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.593
didn't exist when he was president,

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.228
that he didn't build the wall.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.797
And those are the things that Nikki

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.999
Haley is talking about, about the debt

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.200
and how it went up during

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.601
the Trump presidency.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.236
Those are things she is talking about.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.171
And so,

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.839
you know, she's positioning herself,

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:40.873
particularly in New Hampshire,

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:43.076
where independent voters vote

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.211
in the primary as the alternative.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.879
And she's positioning herself

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.882
as somebody who can beat Joe Biden.

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:52.051
Alison, tell us why

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.019
Trump's extreme

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:56.122
extremist rhetoric is not generating

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.123
much more,

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.058
you know, much more condemnation

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.960
from so many in the Republican Party.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.561
Look,

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.363
when you talk privately with Republicans,

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.698
they absolutely condemn that.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.100
The conversation,

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.334
the dialog,

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.336
the divisive rhetoric

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.070
and these comments

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.071
that he's made recently

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:12.572
with regard

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.139
to immigrants

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.874
and poisoning the blood of this country,

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.409
that's disgusting and despicable.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.744
And they will tell you that

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:19.278
many who are supportive of him

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.313
publicly won't

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:21.714
do so forcefully simply

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:22.315
because they don't

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.783
want to face the backlash of him

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:24.884
or his supporters.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:25.485
But I can tell

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:27.720
you, as as Governor Sununu just said,

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.355
that kind of rhetoric

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.757
basically parroting,

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:31.424
as as

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:32.525
many have said, parroting

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:35.261
the words of Hitler from mein camp.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.963
That is wrong and it should not happen.

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.631
And what it does, it really takes away

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.299
from the real conversation

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.267
that Republicans need

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.869
to be having about immigration.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.270
Talking about the Republicans

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.739
actually do support legal immigration.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.540
Talking about what

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.409
we can do to stop the flow of

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.744
of illegal immigrants into this country.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.012
We're seeing record numbers

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.414
stop the flow of fentanyl

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.181
into this country

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.916
as well as human trafficking.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.351
These are serious problems

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.185
with immigration.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.420
And we should be talking about

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.754
and not these stupid comments.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:02.522
Well, it's Americans

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.456
who are bringing fentanyl

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:04.223
in and higher numbers.

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.591
But the point is,

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.026
because Republicans

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.795
won't denounce these comments,

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:11.030
and that keeps Donald Trump

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.064
as the person

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.167
controlling the Republican Party.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:15.435
So this is tolerated.

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.803
And I want to point something out

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.704
about this poisoning the blood rhetoric.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:19.272
And it's something

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.441
I feel very strongly about.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.042
